.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/d3-shape Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "d3-shape"
.PP
Visualizations typically consist of discrete graphical marks, such as \fBsymbols\fP, \fBarcs\fP, \fBlines\fP and \fBareas\fP\&. While the rectangles of a bar chart may be easy enough to generate directly using \fRSVG\fP or \fRCanvas\fP, other shapes are complex, such as rounded annular sectors and centripetal Catmull–Rom splines\&. This module provides a variety of shape generators for your convenience\&.

.PP
As with other aspects of D3, these shapes are driven by data: each shape generator exposes accessors that control how the input data are mapped to a visual representation\&. For example, you might define a line generator for a time series by \fRscaling\fP fields of your data to fit the chart:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const line = d3\&.line()
    \&.x(d => x(d\&.date))
    \&.y(d => y(d\&.value));
.fi
.PP

.PP
This line generator can then be used to compute the \fRd\fP attribute of an SVG path element:

.PP
.PP
.nf
path\&.datum(data)\&.attr("d", line);
.fi
.PP

.PP
Or you can use it to render to a Canvas 2D context:

.PP
.PP
.nf
line\&.context(context)(data);
.fi
.PP

.PP
For more, read \fRIntroducing d3-shape\fP\&.
.SH "Installing"
.PP
If you use npm, \fRnpm install d3-shape\fP\&. You can also download the \fRlatest release on GitHub\fP\&. For vanilla HTML in modern browsers, import d3-shape from jsDelivr:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script type="module">

import {line} from "https://cdn\&.jsdelivr\&.net/npm/d3\-shape@3/+esm";

const l = line();

</script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
For legacy environments, you can load d3-shape’s UMD bundle; a \fRd3\fP global is exported:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src="https://cdn\&.jsdelivr\&.net/npm/d3\-path@3"></script>
<script src="https://cdn\&.jsdelivr\&.net/npm/d3\-shape@3"></script>
<script>

const l = d3\&.line();

</script>
.fi
.PP
